# Precedence

Project rules override these; repository documentation (`/docs`, `README.md`, ADRs) overrides
both. Project conventions beat skill defaults. When no skill applies, say so rather than
inventing a process.

Machine-local specifics — Jira project keys, boards, documentation repositories, cluster names —
live in `~/.cursor/local/`, unversioned (symlinked to `~/.claude/local/`). Read the file a
command or skill names; if it is missing, ask rather than guess.
